\details{
The weight solve is checked against an exact quadratic-programming
solution in the test suite: at convergence it reaches the same objective,
which is at least as low as \code{Synth}'s interior-point solve.

It is deliberately separate from \code{\link[=fit_sdid]{fit_sdid()}} rather than another
\verb{estimator =} branch there. \code{fit_sdid()} delegates to \code{synthdid}, whose
\code{sc_estimate()} matches on pre-period outcomes only and has no bias
correction; bolting predictor matching onto it would change the meaning
of the existing \code{"sc"} option and put every stored run's numbers in play.
